The SELinux policy package (<package>-selinux, RPM only) is the exception.
Its sources in packaging/selinux are Apache-2.0, but the compiled policy
modules contain expansions of the SELinux reference policy macros
(selinux-policy-devel, GPL-2.0-or-later), so that package is distributed
under "Apache-2.0 AND GPL-2.0-or-later" and ships the reference policy's
license text. Its corresponding source is this repository at the release
commit plus the Fedora selinux-policy source package of the version named
in its THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES file. See packaging/selinux/README.
